-- title:
--   Future-matrix entries split between earlier children
-- statement:
--   Fix natural $n,r$, Boolean subset-oracle functions $o_1,o_2$, and a rational parameter $q$. For a paired state $S$, write $\widehat r(S)$ for the value returned by the program's paired-rank routine using $r,o_1,o_2$, and put $f(S)=q^{\,n\mathbin{\dot-}\widehat r(S)}$, with truncated natural subtraction. No correctness promise for the oracles is implicit.
--
--   For paired sets $B,R\subseteq G=[n]\times\{0,1\}$, a set $U\subseteq[n]$, and a displayed hole $e$, let $\mathcal C(B,R,U;e)$ consist of distinct states of the form $B\cup(R\setminus\{e\})\cup\{(u,c_u):u\in U\}$ for choices $c_u\in\{0,1\}$. Define $s_{B,R,U}(e)=\sum_{S\in\mathcal C(B,R,U;e)}f(S)$, viewed as a real number.
--
--   Define $M^a_{B,R,U}(e,e)=0$. For distinct holes $e,g$, let $M^a_{B,R,U}(e,g)$ be the sum of $f(S)$ over distinct states $S=B\cup(R\setminus\{e,g\})\cup\{(a,0),(a,1)\}\cup\{(u,c_u):u\in U\setminus\{a\}\}$. Suppose $t\in U$, $t\ne a$, and both labels of $t$ are absent from $B\cup R$. Put $R_c=R\cup\{(t,c)\}$ and $U'=U\setminus\{t\}$. For all $e,g\in R$,
--
--   $$M^a_{B,R_0,U'}(e,g)+M^a_{B,R_1,U'}(e,g)=M^a_{B,R,U}(e,g).$$
--
--   The future pair $a$ need not itself belong to $U$. This is a weighted counting identity without positivity or matroid hypotheses.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/meelgroup/counting-matroid/blob/dd16a4628fdb095c58fe0f3dfd8e353c6e97443c/CountingMatroid/Analysis/DefectSlotConservation.lean#L179-L215

